# Python-generated files
__pycache__/
*.py[oc]
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.egg-info

# Finder's per-directory state. It is untracked junk that a pre-commit `git add -A` would
# otherwise publish into a public repo's history on the tick it happens to run.
.DS_Store

# Virtual environments
.venv
.pytest_cache/
bench/out/

# onnxruntime-web for the node gate; reinstall with `npm ci`, never commit
node_modules/

# runs/ holds checkpoints and scratch. G7 promises committed witnesses, so the
# small tables (.json/.md/.log) stay tracked; weights directories, *.pt dumps and
# the latency harness's .lock file do not.
runs/*
!runs/*.json
!runs/*.md
!runs/*.log
# ...except the pair driver's own stdout, which `!runs/*.log` above would otherwise pull in:
# its first line echoes the launcher's absolute interpreter path, and the per-arm flat
# witnesses (`runs/antiprior_off_s0.train.log`) are what the registry reads. §9.50's rule.
runs/pair_driver.log
runs/antiprior_on_s0c.driver.log
# same reason as pair_driver.log above: this log echoes the launcher's expanded command, whose
# first token is this laptop's absolute interpreter path.
runs/ckpt_backup_on_s0c.log
runs/ckpt_backup_on_s0c.state

# Derived corpora: the rows are upstream text, so the default is that only the provenance file
# stays in git (it pins revisions, seeds, collision counts and the sha256 of the generated
# train.jsonl). The pilot splits below are the one exception, published on the owner's decision
# (2026-09-30) so a fresh clone can run every registry row whose `--suite` default is
# `data/decision-v2-pilot` — including the Tier 0 row, whose harness reads that path.
data/*
!data/decision-v2-pilot/
data/decision-v2-pilot/*
!data/decision-v2-pilot/upstream_manifest.json
!data/decision-v2-pilot/train.jsonl
!data/decision-v2-pilot/development.jsonl
!data/decision-v2-pilot/test.jsonl
!data/decision-v2-pilot/calibration.jsonl
!data/decision-v2-pilot/tokenizer-8192.json

# The four shipping screenshots are the layout witness and are committed. The int8 set
# is the same page with two red checks — its claim is the byte and probability table in
# runs/browser_g3_int8.json, and `npm run g3 -- --artifact runs/onnx_int8` redraws the
# PNGs on demand, so 4.4 MB of near-duplicate pixels stay out of a 114 KiB repo.
docs/screenshots/int8/

# The corpus staging dirs: `kaggle/package_dataset.py` and the upload recipe copy
# `data/decision-v2-pilot` into one of these before `kaggle datasets create`, so they are
# a ~60 MB duplicate of a corpus that is already a private dataset. A `git add -A` would
# commit the copy as a second corpus and put upstream text in this repo's history.
.kaggle-dataset/
kaggle-dataset/
.local-kaggle-upload/
